{
  "question": "Why do resonator_lab measurements show a modest upward shift (baseline mean 2.6979 → post‑baseline mean 2.7048 cycles/beat, z = 1.51) and a series of higher values on day 28, while the other three instruments remain statistically unchanged?",
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "label": "Instrumental calibration drift or hardware degradation in resonator_lab",
      "probability": 0.30,
      "rationale": "A genuine change in the resonator_lab hardware or its calibration could produce a systematic increase in measured cycles/beat. The post‑baseline mean is higher than the baseline and the day‑28 trials (e.g., 2.7355 cycles/beat) are consistently above the baseline average.",
      "evidenceFor": ["baseline_vs_post_z1.51", "event_726726", "event_980040", "event_938892"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["event_826778", "event_408199", "event_972486", "event_561093", "event_553097", "event_198635"]
    },
    {
      "label": "Statistical fluctuation within expected random variation",
      "probability": 0.35,
      "rationale": "A z‑score of 1.51 corresponds to a two‑tailed p≈0.13, which is not highly improbable for the sample sizes involved. The day‑28 data contain both higher and lower values relative to the baseline, suggesting natural variability rather than a persistent shift.",
      "evidenceFor": ["baseline_vs_post_z1.51", "event_1002529", "event_708808", "event_675039", "event_970269", "event_1039831"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["event_726726", "event_980040", "event_938892"]
    },
    {
      "label": "Data processing or transcription error affecting post‑baseline resonator_lab entries",
      "probability": 0.20,
      "rationale": "A systematic offset introduced during data entry or conversion could raise all resonator_lab values. The anomaly is confined to resonator_lab, which uses a separate logging pipeline from the other instruments, making a selective error plausible.",
      "evidenceFor": ["event_726726", "event_980040", "event_938892", "baseline_vs_post_z1.51"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["event_1002529", "event_708808", "event_675039"]
    },
    {
      "label": "Subtle environmental change (e.g., temperature or pressure) affecting resonator frequency",
      "probability": 0.05,
      "rationale": "If temperature or pressure shifted, the resonator frequency might change. However, no comparable drift appears in resonator_obs or the pendulum instruments, making a localized environmental effect unlikely.",
      "evidenceFor": ["event_726726", "event_980040"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["event_826778", "event_408199", "event_972486", "event_561093", "event_553097", "event_198635"]
    },
    {
      "label": "Residual (unconsidered factor)",
      "probability": 0.10,
      "rationale": "An unknown source (e.g., aging of the resonator crystal, hidden magnetic field, or software bug) could be responsible; currently no direct evidence points to it.",
      "evidenceFor": [],
      "evidenceAgainst": []
    }
  ],
  "residual": 0.10,
  "summaryOfChange": "The prior view emphasized instrumental drift (p=0.55). New day‑28 data show both higher and lower resonator_lab values, and no similar drift in the other three instruments, reducing confidence in a hardware‑only explanation. The moderate z‑score (1.51) and the mixed sign of day‑28 deviations increase the plausibility of random fluctuation, raising its probability to 0.35. A selective data‑entry error remains possible (0.20) because only resonator_lab is affected. Environmental influence is downgraded (0.05) due to lack of corroborating drift elsewhere. A residual category is kept at 0.10 for any yet‑unidentified cause."
}

