{
  "question": "Why do pendulum_lab and resonator_obs measurements exhibit an unusually high correlation (0.941) at a 3‑day offset, far exceeding chance expectations, while all other instrument pairings show no such relationship?",
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "label": "Shared environmental factor (e.g., temperature/pressure) affecting pendulum_lab and resonator_obs with a ~3‑day lag",
      "probability": 0.30,
      "rationale": "A common, slowly varying environmental variable could influence the pendulum period and, after thermal inertia or HVAC propagation, the resonator frequency in the observation chamber three days later. The specificity to this pair suggests the two locations share a subtle environmental coupling not present for the other instruments.",
      "evidenceFor": ["cross_corr_pleg_obs_3d"],
      "evidenceAgainst": []
    },
    {
      "label": "Data‑processing or logging pipeline error that unintentionally aligns pendulum_lab readings with resonator_obs timestamps shifted by three days",
      "probability": 0.45,
      "rationale": "Both instruments use separate logging software. A bug that copies or offsets pendulum_lab values into the resonator_obs file could produce an artificial correlation precisely at the observed lag. This would affect only this pair and not others, matching the pattern seen.",
      "evidenceFor": ["cross_corr_pleg_obs_3d"],
      "evidenceAgainst": []
    },
    {
      "label": "Physical coupling (vibrational or acoustic) between the laboratory where pendulum_lab resides and the observation chamber housing resonator_obs, with a delayed propagation effect",
      "probability": 0.10,
      "rationale": "Mechanical disturbances could travel through the settlement structure, influencing the resonator after a delay due to damping or slow diffusion of stress. Such a mechanism would be unusual but could explain a lagged correlation.",
      "evidenceFor": ["cross_corr_pleg_obs_3d"],
      "evidenceAgainst": []
    },
    {
      "label": "Statistical fluke despite the high correlation statistic",
      "probability": 0.10,
      "rationale": "Even though the chance level for the best offset was ±0.287, extreme values can occur rarely. The correlation might be a rare coincidence arising from the many offsets examined.",
      "evidenceFor": ["cross_corr_pleg_obs_3d"],
      "evidenceAgainst": []
    }
  ],
  "residual": 0.05,
  "summaryOfChange": "Replaced the prior question about a modest upward shift in resonator_lab with a new, higher‑impact anomaly: the 0.941 correlation between pendulum_lab and resonator_obs at a 3‑day offset. Accordingly, the hypothesis set was rebuilt, discarding earlier drift‑focused explanations and introducing new candidates (environmental lag, data‑pipeline error, physical coupling, and statistical fluke). Probabilities were re‑assigned based on the strength and specificity of the observed correlation, ensuring the total sums to one."
}

