  "summaryOfChange": "The core question remains the same, but the hypothesis probabilities have been revised to reflect the strength of the observed 0.943 correlation and the lack of any supporting environmental or mechanical evidence. The logging‑software‑bug hypothesis has been elevated to the most likely explanation (0.55), while the shared‑environment and physical‑coupling hypotheses have been downgraded. A small residual probability is retained for any other unknown systematic. This re‑weighting follows from the new day‑40 data, which show no obvious physical link between the two series, and the fact that no other instrument pairs exhibit comparable lagged correlations."
}
